    <bpmn:process id="W_W3713" name="W3713. Ethics &amp; Integrity Program Strategy &amp; Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual governance planning (links to VS-36/VS-33.1); program review
Frequency: Annual + on change
Volume: Enterprise ethics &amp; integrity program
Owner: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer / Chief Compliance Officer
Participants: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer, CEO/Board Audit &amp; Risk Committee (links to VS-36/VS-21), Legal (links to VS-100.3), HR (links to VS-19/VS-103), Internal Audit (links to VS-21), ABC/AML (links to VS-86), Loss Prevention (links to VS-23), Risk (links to VS-21.2), Cross-Entity (links to VS-72)
Source: workflow W3713 — Ethics &amp; Integrity Program Strategy &amp; Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3713_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3713_Lane1" name="Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3713_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3713_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3713_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3713_Lane2" name="Board Audit Committee">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3713_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3713_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3713_Start4" name="Annual governance planning (links to VS-36/VS-33.1); program review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3713_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3713_Task5" name="Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer define the ethics &amp; integrity program strategy and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer define the ethics &amp; integrity program strategy and governance: scope (all violation types — ABC/AML, fraud/theft, harassment/discrimination, safety/environmental, consumer-protection, antitrust, conflicts, vendor/supply-chain integrity), the framework (ISO 37001 ABMS / 37301 CMS aligned), the speak-up channel strategy (W3715), the operating model (independent of line/HR where needed), and KPIs (report volume, substantiation rate, cycle-time, retaliation incidents, culture-trust score)
Responsible (R): Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): CEO / Board Audit Committee
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3713_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3713_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3713_Task6" name="Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer establish the governance: Ethics &amp; Compliance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer establish the governance: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer authority and independence (reports to the board audit/risk committee per links to VS-36), the Ethics Committee (W3719), the cross-functional investigation model (HR, Legal, LP, ABC, Audit), and integration to ABC (VS-86), audit (VS-21), legal (VS-100), and risk (VS-21.2)
Responsible (R): Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer / Legal / Board
Accountable (A): CEO / Board Audit Committee
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3713_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3713_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3713_Task7" name="Board Audit &amp; Risk Committee ratify the ethics strategy, policy, and authority…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Board Audit &amp; Risk Committee ratify the ethics strategy, policy, and authority, approve the program budget (links to VS-17.4), and set the integrity-objective; communicate the mandate enterprise-wide (links to W3718)
Responsible (R): Board Audit Committee / Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): Board
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3713_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3713_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3713_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3713_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3713_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-158 (ensure whistleblower confidentiality &amp; non-retaliation.) | - operational: board reporting line; operational: all-violation scope
Owner: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer / Chief Compliance Officer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3713_Assoc10" sourceRef="W3713_Annotation9" targetRef="W3713_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
