    <bpmn:process id="W_W3719" name="W3719. Ethics Committee &amp; Case Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Governance cycle; high-severity case; quarterly review
Frequency: Quarterly + on high-severity case
Volume: Ethics Committee oversight
Owner: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer / Ethics Committee Chair
Participants: Ethics Committee (CFO/COO/CHRO/VP Legal &amp; Compliance/Independent), Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer, Board Audit Committee (links to VS-36), Audit (links to VS-21), Risk (links to VS-21.2)
Source: workflow W3719 — Ethics Committee &amp; Case Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3719_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3719_Lane1" name="Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3719_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3719_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3719_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3719_Lane2" name="Ethics Committee Chair">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3719_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3719_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3719_Start4" name="Governance cycle; high-severity case; quarterly review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3719_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3719_Task5" name="Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer convene the Ethics Committee (cross-functional…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer convene the Ethics Committee (cross-functional executive body) to oversee the program: review high-severity/substantiated cases, approve major disciplinary/corrective action (links to W3724), adjudicate conflicts/escalations, and oversee retaliation response (links to W3725)
Responsible (R): Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer / Committee Chair
Accountable (A): Ethics Committee
Duration: Quarterly + on case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3719_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3719_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3719_Task6" name="Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer provide the committee program reporting: report…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer provide the committee program reporting: report volume/intake (W3715), triage/investigation status, substantiation rate, case cycle-time, retaliation incidents, and program KPIs (links to W3729); the committee directs priorities and resources
Responsible (R): Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): Ethics Committee
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3719_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3719_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3719_Task7" name="Ethics Committee report program posture, material cases, and ethics-risk…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Ethics Committee report program posture, material cases, and ethics-risk exposure to the Board Audit &amp; Risk Committee (links to VS-36/VS-21.2) and ensure the program&#x27;s independence, resourcing, and authority are sustained
Responsible (R): Ethics Committee Chair / Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer
Accountable (A): Board Audit Committee
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3719_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3719_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3719_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3719_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3719_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-158 (ensure whistleblower confidentiality &amp; non-retaliation.) | - operational: board mandate and independent membership; operational: escalation protocol
